                                       "message":  "Release v1.5.5: stop source-pool reallocation on overlay jitter\n\nfix(extension): hold the source/mid texture pool size across small overlay\nchanges. The overlay backing is round(rect * DPR), so player chrome, hover\ncontrols or a scrollbar move it by a few px every tick, and\nensureFrameTextures reallocated the entire pool (presentation queue wiped,\nevery texture recreated) on any dimension change - a visible freeze that\nlooked random because it followed page layout. poolDims() stays the pure\n\"what size should the pool be\"; holdPoolDims() dead-bands it against the\nsize committed at the last real reallocation (max(16px, 2%)), so only\ngenuine resizes (fullscreen, theater) reallocate. The blit already scales\npool -\u003e overlay.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 \u003cnoreply@anthropic.com\u003e",
